      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For dead load, you should use the published specific gravity or unit weight for Western Red Cedar for an accurate calculation. Regarding live load in BC, the National Building Code or local municipal bylaws will specify the exact design load, but typical residential decking often requires a minimum live load load of 4.7 to 5.0 kPa (kilopascals) or roughly 100 pounds per square foot (PSF). Always defer to the specific requirements outlined in your permit documents to avoid code violations.",
