      "content": "Inspect the lumber carefully for any signs of rot, significant checking (splitting), or excessive knots, as these reduce strength. Use high-quality, corrosion-resistant fasteners designed for exterior wood to ensure robust metal connections. Proper flashing and sealing around the ledger board are crucial to prevent water intrusion, which is the primary cause of long-term wood decay and strength loss.",
